!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-member-outside-the-facets-beside-it-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §7.4, [TSON-SCHEMA] §7.2"
  description: """
    Every member of a `members` set must satisfy the other facets on the same body, the `pattern`
    included -- the uniform members rule, which the numeric tiers already carry against their bounds
    and step. `nz` does not match `[A-Z]{2}`, so the body admits a member it also refuses, and that
    is a schema-load error rather than something a reader discovers one document at a time.

    This is the one member check in the series that needs a regex match rather than a comparison, so
    an implementation whose constraint model has no regex engine cannot run it beside the others. The
    vector exists because that is exactly the check most likely to be quietly skipped: skipping it
    leaves a type whose declared value set and declared shape disagree, and every value that would
    have shown it up is one the type rejects anyway.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
